SAL -> Yices2 interface
-----------------------

Yices is a SAT and SMT solver developed by SRI International. Yices 1
is the detault backend solver for SAL, and it is used by sal-bmc and
sal-inf-bmc.

Since SAL version 3.2, we have added support for SAL to use the newer
version of Yices, namely Yices 2, that is available at 
http://yices.csl.sri.com/.

To use Yices 2 has backend solver for SAL:

1) download the Yices 2 distribution suitable for your OS at

    http://yices.csl.sri.com/download-yices2.shtml

   then unpack the tarfile in a directory of your choice.

   Unlike Yices 1, the Yices 2 distribution contains different
   executables (yices-sat is the SAT solver, and yices is the 
   SMT solver).

2) Assuming you've installed Yices 2 in a directory such as 
    /home/lambda/yices-2.0.0/  then both Yices 2 solvers will
    be in /home/lambda/yices-2.0.0/bin.

  For SAL to find these solvers at run time: edit (or create) the file 
   .salrc file in your home directory and add the following lines

   (sal/set-yices2-sat-command! "/home/lambda/yices-2.0.0/bin/yices-sat")
   (sal/set-yices2-command! "/home/lambda/yices-2.0.0/bin/yices")

  Adjust this to your own installation. On Cygwin, the Yices 2 solvers
  have an '.exe' suffix.

3) To select Yices 2 instead of Yices 1 when using sal-bmc or sal-inf-bmc,
   use the command-line option -s yices2.

For sal-inf-bmc, SAL now invokes the Yices 2 SMT solver with the
option `--mcsat` so that nonlinear arithmetic can be delegated to
Yices2's MCSAT engine. This requires a Yices2 build compiled with
MCSAT support. If you need to fall back to the classic solver, add

   (sal/set-yices2-mcsat-mode! #f)

to your `.salrc' file.

Native Bigloo bindings
----------------------

Run `make yices2-ffi` after configuring SAL to build the standalone
`yices2-ffi` module. Run `make test-yices2-ffi` to exercise it against
Yices2 and GMP. For a custom installation, pass
`YICES2_PREFIX=/path/to/install`. The
`YICES2_CPPFLAGS`, `YICES2_LDFLAGS`, and `YICES2_LIBS` variables allow separate
header and library locations.

The build runs the Scheme program `src/yices2-ffi-generator.scm` on
`src/yices2_api.spec` to generate the standalone `yices2_ffi.scm` module.
It writes the module and `yices2_ffi.o` to the `yices2-ffi/` object directory.
Add that directory to Bigloo's search path and use
`(import (yices2-ffi "yices2_ffi.scm"))` in the client module. Compile with
the same Yices2 header paths and link `yices2_ffi.o` with the same native
libraries. C names map to Scheme names by replacing underscores with
hyphens. The four build metadata declarations are read-only foreign
variables.

The bindings expose the C API's argument types, return codes, and ownership
rules. Pass explicitly allocated foreign buffers for pointer and array
arguments. `yices-string-copy` and `yices-const-string-copy` copy foreign
strings into Scheme. Release owned Yices strings with `yices-free-string`.
For examples of buffer allocation and context, model, and vector lifetimes,
see `tests/yices2_ffi_test.scm`.

The PVS specification includes some symbols that vary between Yices2 builds.
`(yices-api-missing-functions)` lists those unavailable with the selected
headers and libraries. Calling one of those functions raises a Scheme error.
